# motto eval secrets — copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in what you need.
# `.env` is auto-loaded when running the evals (`npm run evals`); it is NOT used
# by the published plugin or `npm test` (unit specs). Every var is optional —
# the eval harness degrades gracefully: any harness or the judge whose
# credentials are absent is skipped with a stated reason, never a false pass.
# Run `npm run evals:list` to see what's currently runnable.

# --- Master switch --------------------------------------------------------
# Evals call real agent CLIs and cost money. They only run when this is 1.
# RUN_EVALS=1

# --- LLM judge (Cloudflare AI Gateway) ------------------------------------
# Same three-var convention as the other @ikko-dev projects (gitlab-review,
# c24n). The judge routes through the gateway so a *different* model can score
# answers (avoiding self-preference). Fill these from your own Cloudflare
# account/gateway — find the account id in the Cloudflare dashboard URL or under
# AI Gateway; create/point GATEWAY_ID at a gateway of your own.
# CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY=cfut_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=your_cloudflare_account_id
# CLOUDFLARE_GATEWAY_ID=motto
# Judge model in the gateway's provider/model form (default: openai/gpt-5.4-mini):
# EVAL_JUDGE_MODEL=anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5

# --- Agent harness credentials --------------------------------------------
# Each harness gates on its binary being on PATH AND a provider key here.
# Claude Code can also auth via a logged-in session (no key needed then).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-...          # Codex
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=...                  # Pi (its default provider)

# --- Model sweep (optional) -----------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated harness=model overrides; omit to run each harness at its
# default model. Example:
# EVAL_MODELS=claude=claude-opus-4-8,pi=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5
